=========================================================
REM (ROOT EM) UNIT IN CSS
=========================================================

Definition:
rem stands for "root em".
It is a relative unit in CSS.

rem is ALWAYS calculated based on the ROOT element’s
font size (html element).

It does NOT depend on parent elements.

---------------------------------------------------------
WHAT IS THE ROOT ELEMENT?
---------------------------------------------------------

- The root element in HTML is <html>
- By default, browsers set:
  html font-size = 16px

All rem values are calculated using this root value.

---------------------------------------------------------
HOW REM WORKS
---------------------------------------------------------

Formula:
1rem = root font size

Example meaning:
- Root font size = 16px
- 1rem = 16px
- 2rem = 32px
- 0.5rem = 8px

If the root font size changes, ALL rem values update
automatically.

---------------------------------------------------------
REM VS EM (IMPORTANT DIFFERENCE)
---------------------------------------------------------

rem:
- Depends only on root font size
- Same size everywhere
- Easy to manage
- No compounding issue

em:
- Depends on parent font size
- Can compound in nested elements
- Harder to control in large layouts

---------------------------------------------------------
REM FOR FONT SIZE
---------------------------------------------------------

- Most commonly used for font sizes
- Provides consistent typography
- Easy to scale entire website by changing root size

Example meaning:
- If paragraph uses 1rem and root is 16px,
  paragraph text will be 16px everywhere

---------------------------------------------------------
REM FOR SPACING (MARGIN & PADDING)
---------------------------------------------------------

- rem can also be used for:
  * margin
  * padding
  * gap
  * line-height

Benefit:
Spacing scales proportionally with typography.

---------------------------------------------------------
RESPONSIVE DESIGN WITH REM
---------------------------------------------------------

Why rem is powerful:
- Change root font size using media queries
- Entire layout scales automatically

Example meaning:
- Desktop root = 16px
- Mobile root = 14px
- All rem-based elements adjust automatically

---------------------------------------------------------
ADVANTAGES OF REM
---------------------------------------------------------

- Predictable and consistent
- Easy to maintain
- Ideal for responsive typography
- Improves accessibility
- No nesting side effects

---------------------------------------------------------
DISADVANTAGES OF REM
---------------------------------------------------------

- Depends on root font size
- Less control for isolated components
- Requires understanding of root scaling

---------------------------------------------------------
WHEN TO USE REM
---------------------------------------------------------

Use rem when:
- Setting font sizes
- Creating scalable layouts
- Building design systems
- Maintaining consistent spacing

Avoid rem when:
- You need component-level scaling
- Parent-based sizing is required

---------------------------------------------------------
IMPORTANT NOTE
---------------------------------------------------------

Best Practice:
- Use rem for font sizes and spacing
- Use px only when exact control is needed

rem is the most recommended unit for modern,
responsive web typography.
